#
# Topic ACLs. The topic layout is fixed by the backend:
#
#   armx/{site}/{device}/cmd     backend -> device (subscribe-only for the device)
#   armx/{site}/{device}/state   device  -> backend (publish-only for the device)
#   armx/{site}/{device}/event   device  -> backend, one-shot notifications
#
# The LLM never chooses a topic: tools resolve a device through the allowlisted linked-device
# record and the backend builds the topic from that record.

# The API/worker identity: everything under the deployment's site prefix.
user armx-api
topic readwrite armx/#

# A relay node may publish only its own state/events and read only its own command topic.
# Add one block per provisioned device; replace {site}/{device} with the real values.
user esp32-livingroom
topic write armx/home/livingroom/state
topic write armx/home/livingroom/event
topic read  armx/home/livingroom/cmd

user esp32-bedroom
topic write armx/home/bedroom/state
topic write armx/home/bedroom/event
topic read  armx/home/bedroom/cmd

# Home Assistant bridges the same entities; it is treated as a broker client, not a device.
user home-assistant
topic readwrite armx/#
